<title>UK: Hyder sees windfall tax cost 280 mln stg.</title>
<headline>Hyder sees windfall tax cost 280 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>British multi-utility Hyder Plc on Thursday estimated the UK government's windfall tax will cost the company about 280 million stg.</p>
<p>The company was responding to the Labour government's decision to raise 5.2 billion stg through a tax on privatised utilities.</p>
<p>The tax will be based on the difference between the value of companies at privatisation and a calculation related to net profits up to the first four years after sell-off.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4019</p>
